1. 🔄 Activity Counts (4 Features)
These track how many updates were made by teenagers and adults across both streams:

bio_age_5_17: Biometric updates (Age 5–17).
bio_age_17_: Biometric updates (Age 17+).
demo_age_5_17: Demographic updates (Age 5–17).
demo_age_17_: Demographic updates (Age 17+).
👥 2. Census Volume (3 Features)
The base enrollment numbers for the district: 5. age_0_5: Infants/Children enrollment. 6. age_5_17: Youth enrollment. 7. age_18_greater: The primary adult enrollment count.

📊 3. Calculated Ratios (6 Features)
These are the "Engineered" features that provide the most predictive power: 8. dependency_ratio: Child-to-adult burden. 9. children_ratio: Percentage of children in the district. 10. adult_ratio: Percentage of adults in the district. 11. youth_ratio: Percentage of teenagers in the district. 12. aging_index: The ratio indicating a maturing population. 13. bio_demo_ratio: The balance of Biometric vs. Demographic security updates.

📍 4. Location Context (2 Features)
These tell the AI "where" the data is coming from: 14. state_encoded: The numeric ID for the State/UT. 15. district_encoded: The numeric ID for the District.

📅 5. Temporal Context (2 Features)
These tell the AI "when" the activity happened: 16. month: The month of the year (detects seasonal peaks). 17. year: The year of the record.


